
---

### `backend/manage.py`

- Can be used as the Django entry point.
- It loads `config.settings` as the default settings module.

---

## The Odds API Integration Status

**Provider:** The Odds API  
**API Key:** currently used through environment variable:  
`ODDS_API_KEY=245cab3c5cff52364fa847df4171e64f`

### What works
- `python manage.py sync_sports` – successfully imports available sports.
- `python manage.py sync_odds` – now tolerates 404/422 errors and can sync a single sport.
- The provider class exposes `fetch_sports`, `fetch_matches`, `fetch_scores`.

### What has not been fully verified end‑to‑end yet
- A full run of `sync_odds` over all 86 sports was manually interrupted.
- A full run of `sync_results` was also manually interrupted while iterating all sports.
- Some events may return no odds; some sports are temporarily inactive.
- The Odds API free tier only gives **~500 requests/month**, so frequent full syncs will exhaust the quota quickly.

### Recommended usage during development
